{"kind":"event","event_id":4554,"event_uid":"01M2K7EPAAHY02AYYKPDG3C5DR","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":31,"project_uid":"01M2HBYF26YQWA0S07E1J3NSGF","project_name":"popmechanic-ultrapowers","issue_id":216,"issue_uid":"01M2K7CQVHTA4MBYXR2S136A4X","issue_short_id":"6a4x","actor":"exam:1@run-152","hlc_physical_ms":1789499234634,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"ca1eb05acbb8c75d7e4b3ece94865f52b5a7afd3141c25159ab9537ca338b9c3","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2K7EPA8R6NWCMVFAX8P2CAW","author":"exam:1@run-152","body":"exam-1: writing tests/test_fold_wave_anchor.py. Approach: a pytest file that builds a temp git repo with git subprocesses (BASE commit a.txt=l1..l8 + b.txt, head H1 on top), captures a task patch with git diff from a BASE worktree, and drives skills/ultrapowers/kernel/fold_wave.py's fold/resolve/materialize as subprocesses. One test per Proof leg (a..g), each named for its Machine clause. For leg (b) I will freeze the BASE kernel's reading of a two-task same-anchor wave as literals computed by running the BASE kernel now, before any edit.","created_at":"2026-09-15T19:07:14.632802059Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-15T19:07:14.634Z"}
{"kind":"event","event_id":4555,"event_uid":"01M2K7J4DQYW48QJYYZ9TWMFB9","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":31,"project_uid":"01M2HBYF26YQWA0S07E1J3NSGF","project_name":"popmechanic-ultrapowers","issue_id":216,"issue_uid":"01M2K7CQVHTA4MBYXR2S136A4X","issue_short_id":"6a4x","actor":"impl:1@run-152","hlc_physical_ms":1789499347383,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"72a6a0fed9b34c6557e2fa6aedcd2ed011778c2331c0ae44c477a7b24efdff89","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2K7J4DNADVB7B1F4VSP8RXB","author":"impl:1@run-152","body":"Approach for task 1 (anchored patch fold):\n- TaskRef gains a 4th field `anchor` (None = the wave's --base); `_parse_patch` splits an `@<sha>` suffix (last @, only when the left side is an existing file, so a patch path containing @ still parses).\n- `_resolve_tasks` rev-parses the anchor, drops it to None when it equals --base (so the same-anchor path is byte-identical), applies the patch over `anchor or base` and names the anchor in the does-not-apply refusal.\n- `repo_weave.TaskState` gains `anchor_base` (a RepoState, default None). `_fold_text` re-roots the frontier's weave over the anchor's file (`update_state(anchor_base.files[p], current_lines(files[p]))`) before `merge_states`, which makes the merge a three-way over the anchor; `_text_kind`/`_drop_superseded_text`/`_fold_presence` read the anchor base for an anchored task.\n- The frontier base stays the --base snapshot, scoped to the union of each task's OWN touched set (`diff_paths(anchor_i, tree_i)`) — new helper `frontier_fold.union_touched_anchored`.\n- The fold event gains `anchor` only when it differs from the log's base; `rehydrate` reads `e.get('anchor', base)` for both apply_patch_tree and publish. materialize derives its touched set per fold event against that event's anchor.\n- The weave shadow declines an anchored wave (it re-publishes over --base by construction); it only ever writes the sidecar.","created_at":"2026-09-15T19:09:07.381632289Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-15T19:09:07.383Z"}
